{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/service at b697850820b108c2613d61983a48e1f8e18327dd — the merge station's second source exposed over HTTP, now bounded on every path it can take, under ratified proposal c26a7f57 (25981e55) with the security finding from codex's review 730f3bcc (ratified 41d3364c) repaired. Replaces the retired candidate 83bada54 at 3a45e1f2. internal/service/ui.go serves POST /v0/landed: a bounded list of commits in, and for each the answer to whether the mainline already carries it. The browser names commits, never the ref; the service resolves refs/heads/main then refs/heads/master itself and returns the name it used, so the page can say \"landed on main\" rather than inventing it. When no mainline resolves, every answer is unknown with that stated as the reason — not absent, because no branch to compare against is not evidence that nothing landed. Commit names are validated in the storage layer before any process starts, so a ref name arriving where a commit belongs is refused rather than resolved. Nothing is stored: the station asks at render time, because a field somebody types can be stale by hand and one was. What this head repairs: the advertised LandingLimit was enforced on one path out of two. The cap lives in gitstore.Landings, which only the branch that finds a mainline reaches; when neither mainline ref resolved, the handler took its own route and allocated len(input.Commits), echoing every untrusted commit string back with no bound at all. The documented sixteen-item limit therefore held exactly when the repository was in good shape and lapsed on the failure path, which is the easier one for a caller to reach. The cap now runs once, before either path, because the bound belongs to the endpoint rather than to whichever branch happens to answer; a limit that holds only when the happy path runs is not a limit. internal/service/uidist carries the regenerated two-screen browser build. Conditions actually met at this exact head: two endpoint tests. The first drives a real repository with a merged head and an unmerged side branch, asserting the response names the branch, returns one answer per commit in order, reports the merged head landed and the side head absent, and refuses the string \"main\" as a commit because only the server chooses the ref. The second — new for this repair — posts LandingLimit+5 commits at a repository whose only branch is trunk, and requires exactly LandingLimit answers back, each unknown with a reason and no branch named; with the cap removed it returns 21 where 16 are allowed, so the test measures the defect rather than merely passing. gofmt clean, go vet, go test -count=1 ./..., go test -race -count=1 ./..., and the docset gates all pass; make ui at this head leaves git status --porcelain empty, so the committed embed matches the CI-locked build byte-for-byte. Two commits on main bbc81674; the intervening merges changed internal/app, docs/reference/performance.md, README.md and performance/ only, with no file overlap here. Predecessor at this exact path: 874150d7 (#6782) at 889a64a2, to be retired at merge.","body":{"commit":"b697850820b108c2613d61983a48e1f8e18327dd","path":"internal/service"}}